  "evidence": "Original observations show a sustained E-shift (~+15 to +20 MAD) from ~689 to ~712, with clear onset near 689 and return near 712; N and U show smaller but coherent shifts. P1 (685–711) and P2 (686–714) overlap and are too broad/early on onset and late on return. Hypothesis P2 subtraction creates artificial spikes at boundaries, confirming misalignment. The interior (689–712) shows stable offset level without motion—consistent with a genuine temporary platform. No independent permanent step is embedded in this interval.",
